MEASUREMENT AND DECISION -- docs/adr/0048.

FIRST QUESTION (does it hit our own encrypt path, not just rotate?): YES.
File::SOPS->encrypt_file(unencrypted_regex => '^\w+$') over a key cafe+U+00E9
wrote the value READABLE where sops -e with the same flag ENCRYPTS it. No
rotation, no hand editing, no guard involved. A write defect of its own.

FULL SWEEP: 43 (field, pattern, key) rows through sops -e and encrypt_file.
29 disagreed -- 22 of them a secret sops encrypts and we left bare (\w \d \s \B
and all 12 non-ASCII-reachable POSIX classes, plus (?i)ss vs U+00DF), 7 the
other way (\W \D \S \b [[:^alpha:]], encrypted_regex \w and [:alpha:]).
\p{...}, . and [^a] agreed already. After the change 42 of 43 agree.

WHAT RE2 DOES NOT KNOW, AND WHAT SOPS DOES WITH IT: sops does NOT refuse. It
discards the compile error, so the rule silently matches NOTHING -- measured,
--encrypted-regex '(?=f)foo' writes EVERY value of the document in plaintext at
exit 0 under a sops section, and --unencrypted-regex '(?=f)foo' encrypts every
value. The one place sops reports it is a .sops.yaml path_regex ('error parsing
regexp'), used here as an oracle for 137 patterns.

DECISION: (a)+(b)+(c). /a on both patterns -- RE2's answer for the classes, and
it takes the UTF-8 flag out of the decision (ADR 0003). /a and NOT /aa: RE2's
(?i) does fold k->U+212A and s->U+017F, which /aa would break. Refuse a
construct the two dialects do not share (escape-aware, class-aware,
whitelist-shaped). Refuse a pattern PERL cannot compile with its reason ((?U)
is RE2's and not Perl's). The refusal is raised at USE, not at parse, so
decrypt and extract still read such a document -- verified against one sops
wrote.

CORPUS: 15_960 rule decisions from this suite's own 11 patterns x 653 keys x 2
fields. 18 moved, every one a non-ASCII key under ^\w+$, ZERO ASCII keys.

RESIDUALS -> karr #165: full case folding ((?i)^ss$ vs U+00DF), $ before a
trailing newline, \p{NAME} Go does not have. Handed on: #162 (cpanfile perl
floor -- use re '/a' needs 5.014), #163 (SOPS.pm rotate POD still says this is
open), #164 (two RE2 detectors), #166 (refusal reported under a leaf path).

